[{"id":3031099941,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc60quol","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. Code looks good to me.\r\n\r\nBefore | After\r\n-|-\r\n<img width=\"248\" height=\"287\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/347864e4-93d4-4385-9d4c-1ff2db4f7c63\" /> | <img width=\"248\" height=\"287\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/87aca559-e26b-4bf7-a1d8-0e1722b5c70f\" />\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- You can use EditorSpinSlider's `set_suffix()` method, so that the `°` (degree) and `%` signs can be directly part of the slider. In C++, use `U\"°\"` to enter the degree sign in a string.\r\n  - Once this is done, you can remove `(deg.)` and `(%)` from the rotation/scale snap heading strings.\r\n- There are no buttons to revert to the default value (like in the inspector), but this wasn't present before either.\r\n- The translate snap step should be reduced to `0.001`, so that you can enter values like `0.125` units.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106684#pullrequestreview-3031099941","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106684","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-07-17T21:34:59Z"},{"id":3031100317,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc60quud","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc